    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Perceptron is a small API only family from Perceptron, with 2 versions listed in the OpenRouter catalog, the first from 2026-05-12 and the newest, Perceptron Mk1.5, from 2026-09-25. Both versions support reasoning, and none publish open weights. Context windows run from 32768 to 36864 tokens, and maximum output is 8192 tokens. Input can be audio, image, text or video, while output is text only. Pricing is $0.15 per million input tokens and $1.5 per million output tokens. The facts suggest the family suits multimodal work that benefits from reasoning, such as reading audio, images or video and returning written answers, within a modest context. Limits are the API only access, the small context and output ceiling, and the higher output price relative to input.",
